# Prisma v7 Performance Rules

## 1. Single PrismaClient — Never Instantiate in Services

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — creates a new connection pool per injection
private prisma = new PrismaClient();

// ✅ GOOD — inject the shared DbContext
constructor(private readonly db: DbContext) {}
```

## 2. No N+1 Queries

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — 1 + N queries
const orders = await this.db.order.findMany();
for (const order of orders) {
  const items = await this.db.orderItem.findMany({ where: { orderId: order.id } });
}

// ✅ GOOD — single query
const orders = await this.db.order.findMany({ include: { items: true } });
```

## 3. Always `select` Specific Fields on findMany

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — returns all columns, including blobs and secrets
const users = await this.db.user.findMany();

// ✅ GOOD — only what the caller needs
const users = await this.db.user.findMany({
  select: { id: true, email: true, name: true },
});
```

## 4. Keyset Pagination — Avoid Prisma's Built-in Cursor on Large Tables

Prisma cursor + skip + take + orderBy has a known bug (issue #27094) that omits `LIMIT`, causing full table scans.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — may OOM on large tables (no LIMIT generated)
const page = await this.db.product.findMany({
  cursor: { id: lastId },
  skip: 1,
  take: 20,
  orderBy: [{ createdAt: 'desc' }, { id: 'desc' }],
});

// ✅ GOOD — explicit keyset bounds always produce a LIMIT
const page = await this.db.product.findMany({
  take: 20,
  orderBy: [{ createdAt: 'desc' }, { id: 'desc' }],
  where: {
    OR: [
      { createdAt: { lt: lastRow.createdAt } },
      { createdAt: { equals: lastRow.createdAt }, id: { lt: lastRow.id } },
    ],
  },
});
```

## 5. `relationLoadStrategy: 'join'` for Relation Queries

Collapses related data into a single SQL query. Do **not** use with `cursor`.

```typescript
// ✅ Single SQL with LATERAL JOIN
const posts = await this.db.post.findMany({
  relationLoadStrategy: 'join',
  include: { author: true, tags: true },
  where: { published: true },
  take: 20,
});
```

## 6. Aggregate on the DB, Not in Memory

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const all = await this.db.order.findMany();
const count = all.length;

// ✅ GOOD
const count = await this.db.order.count({ where: { status: 'PENDING' } });
```

## 7. Parallel Reads with Promise.all

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — sequential, wastes time
const users = await this.db.user.findMany(...);
const products = await this.db.product.findMany(...);

// ✅ GOOD — concurrent
const [users, products] = await Promise.all([
  this.db.user.findMany({ select: { id: true, email: true } }),
  this.db.product.findMany({ select: { id: true, price: true } }),
]);
```
